IMPORT prelude

-- Acts Interpretation Act 1901 (Australia): PART 2, the subsections pass 1 left inert (pass 2).
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively. Pass 1 read 2C(2), 2CA(2), 2F(2) and (3), 2K(2), 2L and 2M(3) as rules "already given" by the
-- subsection above them, as widening an official's power, as a judgment, or as a pointer to a document outside the text. Each says
-- something a person can test, and each is encoded here. 2F(6)'s last sentence and 2F(7) are encoded as a rule about an adoption.
-- The rules that pass 1 encoded for these sections are in au-part2-definitions.l4 and au-interpretation-time.l4.

§ `Part 2: Definitions (the subsections that complete ss 2C to 2M)`

§§ `Section 2C(2): express references to companies`

-- src:158 | (2) Express references in an Act to companies, corporations or bodies corporate do not imply that expressions in that Act, of the kind mentioned in subsection (1), do not include companies, corporations or bodies corporate.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 2C(2) (src:158)
GIVEN `the Act expressly refers to companies, corporations or bodies corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the expression is of the kind mentioned in subsection (1), denoting persons generally` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the express reference implies that the expression excludes bodies corporate` `the Act expressly refers to companies, corporations or bodies corporate` `the expression is of the kind mentioned in subsection (1), denoting persons generally` MEANS
    IF `the Act expressly refers to companies, corporations or bodies corporate` AND `the expression is of the kind mentioned in subsection (1), denoting persons generally`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Section 2CA(2): the spouse definition adds to the Act's own`

-- The Example: an Act defines spouse to include a de facto partner and a former spouse. Because of s 2CA, a reference to a person's
-- spouse also covers any person legally married to the person.
-- src:161 | (2) Subsection (1) has effect in addition to any provision of an Act that affects the meaning of spouse in a provision of that Act.
-- src:162 | Example: Spouse is defined for the purposes of an Act to include a de facto partner and a former spouse. Because of this section, a reference in the Act to a person’s spouse covers any person who is legally married to the person, in addition to any person covered by the definition in the Act.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 2CA(2) (src:161-162)
GIVEN `the person is legally married to the other person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Act's own provision about the meaning of spouse covers the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a reference to the spouse in the Act covers the person` `the person is legally married to the other person` `the Act's own provision about the meaning of spouse covers the person` MEANS
    `the person is legally married to the other person` OR `the Act's own provision about the meaning of spouse covers the person`

§§ `Section 2F(2), (3), (6) and (7): the circumstances of a relationship, and adoption`

DECLARE `Circumstance of a relationship` IS ONE OF
    `the duration of the relationship`
    `the nature and extent of their common residence`
    `whether a sexual relationship exists`
    `the degree of financial dependence or interdependence, and any arrangements for financial support, between them`
    `the ownership, use and acquisition of their property`
    `the degree of mutual commitment to a shared life`
    `the care and support of children`
    `the reputation and public aspects of the relationship`
    `another circumstance of their relationship`
    `something that is no circumstance of their relationship`

-- src:174 | (2) In determining for the purposes of paragraph (1)(c) whether 2 persons have a relationship as a couple, all the circumstances of their relationship are to be taken into account, including any or all of the following circumstances:
-- src:175 | (a) the duration of the relationship;
-- src:176 | (b) the nature and extent of their common residence;
-- src:177 | (c) whether a sexual relationship exists;
-- src:178 | (d) the degree of financial dependence or interdependence, and any arrangements for financial support, between them;
-- src:179 | (e) the ownership, use and acquisition of their property;
-- src:180 | (f) the degree of mutual commitment to a shared life;
-- src:181 | (g) the care and support of children;
-- src:182 | (h) the reputation and public aspects of the relationship.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 2F(2) (src:174-182)
GIVEN circumstance IS A `Circumstance of a relationship`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`must be taken into account in deciding whether they have a relationship as a couple` circumstance MEANS
    NOT (circumstance EQUALS `something that is no circumstance of their relationship`)

-- src:183 | (3) No particular finding in relation to any circumstance mentioned in subsection (2) is necessary in determining whether 2 persons have a relationship as a couple for the purposes of paragraph (1)(c).
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 2F(3) (src:183)
GIVEN circumstance IS A `Circumstance of a relationship`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a particular finding about it is necessary` circumstance MEANS
    CONSIDER circumstance
    WHEN `another circumstance of their relationship` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `something that is no circumstance of their relationship` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:192 | For this purpose, disregard whether an adoption is declared void or has ceased to have effect.
-- src:193 | (7) For the purposes of subsection (6), adopted means adopted under the law of any place (whether in or out of Australia) relating to the adoption of children.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 2F(6) and (7) (src:192-193)
GIVEN `it was an adoption under the law of a place relating to the adoption of children` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that place is in or out of Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the adoption has been declared void` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the adoption has ceased to have effect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`counts as an adoption for the purposes of subsection (6)` `it was an adoption under the law of a place relating to the adoption of children` `that place is in or out of Australia` `the adoption has been declared void` `the adoption has ceased to have effect` MEANS
    `it was an adoption under the law of a place relating to the adoption of children`

§§ `Section 2K(2): rules of court`

-- src:222 | (2) The power of the authority to make rules of court includes a power to make rules of court for the purpose of any Act which directs or authorises anything to be done by rules of court.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 2K(2) (src:222)
GIVEN `the Act directs or authorises anything to be done by rules of court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the power to make rules of court includes a power to make them for the purpose of the Act` `the Act directs or authorises anything to be done by rules of court` MEANS
    IF `the Act directs or authorises anything to be done by rules of court` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Section 2L: references to Australian Standards`

DECLARE `A reference to a standard` HAS
    `its words`   IS A STRING
    `its letters` IS A STRING
    `its number`  IS A STRING

DECLARE `A standard` HAS
    `its number`    IS A NUMBER
    `published by`  IS A STRING

-- src:223 | 2L References to Australian Standards
-- src:224 | In any Act, a reference consisting of the words “Australian Standard” followed by the letters “AS” and a number is a reference to the standard so numbered that is published by, or on behalf of, Standards Australia.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 2L (src:223-224)
GIVEN reference IS A `A reference to a standard`
GIVETH A MAYBE `A standard`
`the standard the reference is a reference to` reference MEANS
    IF reference's `its words` EQUALS "Australian Standard" AND reference's `its letters` EQUALS "AS"
    THEN CONSIDER TONUMBER (reference's `its number`)
         WHEN JUST n THEN JUST (`A standard` OF n, "Standards Australia")
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Section 2M(3): what counts as an adjournment`

DECLARE `House of the Parliament` IS ONE OF `the Senate`, `the House of Representatives`

DECLARE `Way a sitting of a House ends` IS ONE OF
    `the House adjourns`
    `the Parliament is prorogued`
    `the House is dissolved`
    `the House expires`

-- src:230 | (3) For the purposes of this section, a House is taken to have adjourned if:
-- src:231 | (a) the Parliament is prorogued; or
-- src:232 | (b) that House is dissolved; or
-- src:233 | (c) if that House is the House of Representatives—that House expires.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 2M(3) (src:230-233)
GIVEN house IS A `House of the Parliament`
      end IS A `Way a sitting of a House ends`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the House is taken to have adjourned` house end MEANS
    CONSIDER end
    WHEN `the House adjourns` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `the Parliament is prorogued` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `the House is dissolved` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `the House expires` THEN IF house EQUALS `the House of Representatives` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
